cff-version: 1.2.0
title: draft
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it using
  these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sebastien
    family-names: Rousseau
    email: sebastian.rousseau@gmail.com
    orcid: null
repository-code: https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/draft
url: https://draftlib.com
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool and Go library that turns research papers into
  publication-ready Markdown drafts in which every sentence is grounded
  in a fact it can prove. Claims are mined from the source and admitted
  only when their supporting quote occurs verbatim in it, so the model
  that writes the article never sees an unverified fact.
keywords:
  - grounded-generation
  - hallucination-prevention
  - claim-verification
  - document-processing
  - golang
  - command-line-tool
  - local-first
license: MIT OR Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.33
